      },
      "body": "So currently there is an option to show an icon on the workspace that is currently active, so basically where your cursor is. But instead i want the icon to show what workspace is assigned to the monitor that the waybar is on. \nFor example my cursor is on monitor 2 and I want to see which workspace is on monitor 1. Currently I would have to move my cursor to that monitor to find out. It would be great if I could find that out just by looking at the waybar that is on monitor 1.\nThis would be very useful for people with multiple monitors that are also using \"focusworkspaceoncurrentmonitor\" dispatcher on hyprland.",
