      },
      "body": "Is there a way to make it so waybar only shows active workspaces? I have 4 persistent workspaces set for my secondary and primary displays and when I try to split them with the clock in between, it keeps adding the active workspaces to the persistent work spaces. \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a56c6b2d-080f-460c-8cb0-794572e0c69a)\n\n```\n    \"hyprland/workspaces\": {\n        \"format\": \"{icon}\",\n        \"format-icons\": {\n            \"active\": \"\",\n            \"default\": \"\"\n        },\n        \"persistent-workspaces\": {\n            \"*\": [ 1,2,3,4 ] // workspace 1 shown on DP-3\n        },\n        \"ignore-workspaces\": [5,6,7,8]\n    },\n    \"hyprland/workspaces#2\": {\n        \"format\": \"{icon}\",\n        \"format-icons\": {\n            \"active\": \"\",\n            \"default\": \"\"\n        },\n        \"persistent-workspaces\": {\n            \"*\": [ 5,6,7,8 ] // workspace 1 shown on DP-3\n        },\n        \"ignore-workspaces\": [1,2,3,4]\n    }\n```",
