      "body": "## Issue\r\n\r\nHey everyone.\r\n\r\nI really appreciate the work that y'all have done with the `hyprland` module. I've been tracking it for a while, and it's come a long way in a little time. Great work!\r\n\r\nAfter the last commit, I've noticed that the `#workspaces button.active` CSS decorator is not working for me when paired with `persistent_workspaces` after the addition of `#workspaces button.visible`.\r\n\r\nHere's my workflow:\r\n* I have 7 persistent workspaces (1-7) shown on each of my three monitors (persistent workspaces colored blue via `#workspaces button.persistent`)\r\n* The workspaces that are currently visible on each monitor are colored orange (via the new `#workspaces button.visible` CSS)\r\n* What I want is the currently active workspace to be colored green\r\n\r\nIt's the last part that is not happening; the active workspace is not currently being colored according to the CSS I have set. I've tried all combinations of `all-outputs` and `active-only` and the end result is the same. The monitors that are visible on each workspace are correctly being colored orange (or blue if I remove the `#workspaces button.visible from CSS), but the active workspace is not being colored green.\r\n\r\nMy config file and CSS are attached. I'm not sure if there is a CSS priority and that active is the last on the list or not triggering properly, or if I'm just missing something obvious. I'm a SQL developer, so after spending all day looking at code for work, my brain is probably fried and I might be missing something.\r\n\r\nAgain, thanks for all the awesome work on this module. Y'all are great!\r\n[config.txt](https://github.com/Alexays/Waybar/files/12528834/config.txt)\r\n[style.txt](https://github.com/Alexays/Waybar/files/12528836/style.txt)\r\n\r\n\r\n## System\r\n* Arch Linux (kernel 6.4.12)\r\n* Waybar v0.9.22-39-g80de22a1 (branch 'master') (using `waybar-git` from AUR)",
